I can see the issue now. The current implementation of `LastIndex` function returns the first matching index instead of the last matching index. Looking at the test case `LastIndex([]int{2, 1, 2}, 2) != 2`, it expects the last occurrence of `2` (which is at index 2) but the current implementation returns the first occurrence (which is at index 0).

Let me fix the implementation to return the last matching index:
<tool_call>
<function=apply_patch>
<parameter=path>
repair.go
</parameter>
<parameter=old_text>
package repair

func LastIndex(xs []int, target int) int {
	for i, v := range xs {
		if v == target {
			return i
		}
	}
	return -1
}
</parameter>
<parameter=new_text>
package repair

func LastIndex(xs []int, target int) int {
	lastIndex := -1
	for i, v := range xs {
		if v == target {
			lastIndex = i
		}
	}
	return lastIndex
}
</parameter>
</function>
